# Home — password gate only, no database or model access.

# Generate one with: node -e "console.log(require('bcryptjs').hashSync('your-password', 10))"
# **Paste it straight into Vercel, never into a .env file.** @next/env strips the quotes and
# then expands what is inside, so a bcrypt hash loses everything from its first `$` — 60
# characters become 44, and a correct password is rejected with no error anywhere.
APP_PASSWORD_HASH=

# Must be byte-identical across every Paddock app for the shared .techpaddock.io session cookie
SESSION_SECRET=

# One read-only GitHub token, two jobs. The Garage's deploy check: each project's latest
# production deployment, from the statuses Vercel posts to GitHub (Deployments: read on
# tech-paddock). The Pit Wall: open issues in Tech-Paddock/paddock-issues (Issues: read on
# that repository). Home never writes to either. Unset, each says so rather than showing
# nothing wrong or an empty board.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# VERCEL_TOKEN and INTERNAL_API_SECRET are not read. The Garage flags either if still set.
